  "worked_solution": "The centroid of a lamina $D$ with area ${A}_{D}$ is given by $({x}_{c},{y}_{c}),$ where\n\n$$\n{x}_{c}=\\frac{1}{{A}_{D}}{\u222c}_{D}x\\,\\,\\text{d}A,\\,{y}_{c}=\\frac{1}{{A}_{D}}{\u222c}_{D}y\\,\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nNotice that $D$ is a type I plane region:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073832/assets/536f542f535513430311b29f43f6fbafb37832d6dfde3b9c81e82237cb011821.png)\n\nSo, we have \n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,-2\\le x\\le 2,\\,0\\le y\\le 4-{x}^{2}}\n$$\n\nand ${A}_{D}=\\frac{32}{3}.$\n\nTherefore, the $y$-coordinate of the centroid is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{c} & =\\frac{1}{{A}_{D}}{\u222c}_{D}y\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{32}{\\int }_{-2}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{4-{x}^{2}}y\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{32}{\\int }_{-2}^{2}{[\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}]}_{y=0}^{y=4-{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{64}{\\int }_{-2}^{2}(16-8{x}^{2}+{x}^{4})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{64}{[16x-\\frac{8{x}^{3}}{3}+\\frac{{x}^{5}}{5}]}_{-2}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{64}[(32-\\frac{64}{3}+\\frac{32}{5})-(-32+\\frac{64}{3}-\\frac{32}{5})] \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
